Origin: EmberBSD; Rust 1.100.0 stage0 std for a requested host target; not submitted upstream.

On an EmberBSD host, the Rust host triple is also the target triple.
Std::run never builds a stage0 std for the host triple, so x.py planned
no library build. With local-rebuild=true, build the std when the run
requests the host triple as a target, and link it into stage0-sysroot
instead of the std of the initial sysroot. Host tools of the initial
sysroot stay. Builds for other targets are unchanged.
Rust source licenses and upstream identifiers are preserved.

